<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 69,228 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 69,228 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 69,228 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 30,427 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   August 5</p>
<p>    Export cargo		10,711	 9,990</p>
<p>    Import cargo		58,517	20,437</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ship sailed and nine berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	    67,658	 Johar		     Due</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	18,600	 Kristal		   Due</p>
<p>Palm oil		7,775	 Fossanger		 7/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
